The paper rules out the triage idea as stated: it does not present an “automata decision” theorem for oscillator reconfiguration. Its executable constructions are (i) disjoint noninteracting oscillators whose joint period is an LCM (§2.4), and (ii) Snark loops for every period \(p\ge 43\) (§2.5.2). I’m testing a native Track B family built around the LCM construction, because direct oscillator search is explicitly solver-driven (§§2.3, 2.6, 2.7) and would not support an honest Track A claim for a planted distribution.
